**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/*.log
**/.env
**/.env.*
.git
.husky

# The GeoLite2 db is mounted at runtime, never needed in the build context
**/geodata
*.mmdb

# Downloaded source corpora — 575 MB of JMdict, KANJIDIC, KanjiVG, Tatoeba and
# wiktextract. Nothing COPYs them, so they never reach an image, but Docker
# uploads the whole context to the daemon before the first instruction runs.
# Importers re-download on demand and are meant to run on a laptop anyway.
.data

# Media. The R2 assets bucket is the single source for both trees (see DEPLOY.md
# "Assets on R2"), so neither belongs in an image: the audio is ~11,000 clips
# and ~90 MB regenerated by `audio:all`, the images are hand-drawn SVGs whose
# source stays in git. Both are pushed with `upload:assets`.
#
# There is deliberately NO origin fallback left. R2_PUBLIC_BASE_URL is required
# — the backend refuses to boot in production without it — because a silent
# miss would 404 every clip and illustration while the pages around them keep
# working, which is the hardest kind of breakage to spot.
#
# Everything else in public/ (favicon, PWA icons, manifest, robots.txt) is tiny
# and must stay: it is what the browser asks for before any API call.
nihongo/frontend/public/audio
nihongo/frontend/public/images
